From abf3d1b11c3da8df1ea2ddf267a3618aaccaeef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:20:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Merge branch 'partners-npc-c' into integration

Conflicts resolved keeping every branch:
- per-partner rows, VLALL, TRN/TRN2 ids: all rows;
- ids.h: npc-c's ids (Gigadramon defined once), HAS_RAISED_FLAG with every
  partner that has a flag, RAISED_TRIGGER kept;
- file_table_us.c: DIGI.DAT and MUGP/JIJP/ANLP.MMD before NULL, the size
  from the initializer;
- model.c: species' getDigimonModelName/getDigimonModelRef and npc-c's
  partner-only names (class 3), whose fallback is the species name; the async
  read uses DIGI.DAT sectors, the FILE_OFFSET_TABLE lookup for a partner
  file, or the CHDAT path;
- tickConditions: one Ultimate branch, Machinedramon (48 h) first, then a
  path target (MetalEtemon, 96 h); npc-a's type guards dropped since
  getEvolutionPath gives every type a row (new species keep evolving);
- efe.c: npc-c's bone maps folded into the one MOD_TECH_DONORS table;
- mod_lab.c: one evolve list.

